Fix: the pending-insertion policy applies to the paragraphs a patch edits

Regression from the absorption change (ADR 0047). On a real patent workdir
(which contains eight pending insertions) a patch to an ordinary paragraph was
refused:

    edit-inside-pending-insertion: P101 is a pending insertion by '照轩 林';
    an edit by '' would have to be recorded as a revision inside it ...

Two defects in one line of policy:

- the check ran for EVERY pending insertion in the document instead of the
  paragraphs the caller edited, so one untouched insertion vetoed the whole
  patch;
- in direct mode there is no revision context, so the author resolved to '' and
  every insertion looked foreign. Direct mode synthesises no revisions, so
  there is nothing to refuse there in the first place.

plan_sync now takes `edited_ids` (the set the caller actually changed) and the
policy runs only for those, and only when a session author exists. `None` means
"unknown", where the policy stays out of the way and the post-plan check still
refuses a nested shape. The tool layer supplies the set: document_patch from its
applied hunks, document_replace from the paragraphs it matched.

Verification: the real workdir patches P29 again (OK), while an edit by another
author inside an actual pending insertion is still refused; 10 passed in
tests/test_insertion_chain.py (new regression: a document that merely contains
another author's insertion stays editable), 138 passed across
test_mcp_server/test_edit_sync/test_patch_properties.
